<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vienna (1683)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1683">1683</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as failed Vienna siege of 1683 · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> was fought in 1683, when a relief army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III Sobieski of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> broke the Ottoman siege of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> capital. The failed siege ended the westward advance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>. It was followed by a long war in which the Ottomans lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, and is often treated as the start of Ottoman decline.</p></div>
